# Astronomer

> Astronomer empowers data teams to enhance their data availability with Astro, a modern data orchestration platform powered by Apache Airflow. Astro enables companies to place Airflow at the core of their data operations, providing ease of use, scalability, and enterprise-grade security to ensure the reliable delivery of mission-critical data pipelines.

All blog posts on this site are available as clean Markdown by appending `.md` to the post URL.
For example: `https://www.astronomer.io/blog/post-slug.md`

## Developer Resources

- [OpenAPI spec](https://www.astronomer.io/.well-known/openapi.json): Machine-readable OpenAPI 3.1 specification for the Astronomer marketing site function API (Mux upload helpers).
- [API catalog](https://www.astronomer.io/.well-known/api-catalog): RFC 9264 linkset JSON listing all service endpoints, OpenAPI spec location, and health check URL.
- [MCP server card](https://www.astronomer.io/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json): Model Context Protocol server discovery card for WebMCP tool access.
- [Agent skills index](https://www.astronomer.io/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json): Discoverable agent skill manifests for site navigation and function API usage.
- [Health / status](https://www.astronomer.io/.well-known/status): Live health-check endpoint (application/health+json).
- [Authentication docs](https://docs.astronomer.io/astro/automation-authentication): API authentication guide for Astro platform API access.
- [Astro API reference](https://docs.astronomer.io/astro/api): REST API reference for the Astro data orchestration platform.

## Blog

- [The Astro Runtime: Airflow re-engineered for speed and scale](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/astro-airflow-re-engineered-for-speed-and-scale.md): Open-source Airflow finds ready work on a timer; Astro gets a hint. 100x lower p95 task-start latency at twice the load, on the same database and interfaces.
- [How We Built Cross-Region Disaster Recovery for Astro on Azure](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/how-we-built-cross-region-disaster-recovery-for-astro-on-azure.md): Disaster Recovery on Azure is now generally available on Astro
- [The New Astro Runtime](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/the-new-astro-runtime.md): We rebuilt Airflow's scheduler, executor, and infrastructure on Astro: 500,000 concurrent tasks, 228ms task starts, and the same DAGs you run today.
- [How We Built Cross-Region Disaster Recovery for Astro on Google Cloud](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/how-we-built-cross-region-disaster-recovery-for-astro-on-google-cloud.md): How we built it Cross-region disaster recovery on GCP: the architecture, the decisions specific to Google Cloud, and what teams need to plan before starting.
- [Debunking myths about Airflow’s use cases](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/debunking-myths-about-airflows-use-cases.md): Learn the truth about time-based scheduling limitations, ML/AI workflow compatibility, streaming processing, and whether Airflow is outdated technology.
- [Debunking myths about the Airflow user experience](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-fact-vs-fiction-part-1-airflow-user-experience.md): Debunking some common Apache Airflow misconceptions
- [Debunking myths about Airflow’s architecture and performance](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/debunking-myths-about-airflows-architecture-and-performance.md): In this second post, we’ll turn our attention to another common theme in discussions about Airflow: its architecture and performance.
- [A redesigned Astro for teams managing at scale: one view across every workspace, deployment, and pipeline](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/a-redesigned-astro-for-teams-managing-at-scale-one-view-across-every-workspace-deployment-and-pipeline.md): Built for teams managing multiple workspaces, Astro's redesigned navigation puts your entire org in one view the moment you log in.
- [Introducing Apache Airflow® 3.3](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/introducing-apache-airflow-3-3.md): Better failure handling with the task state store, pluggable retries, and more
- [The Airflow Build vs. Buy Question We See Data Leaders Get Wrong](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/the-airflow-build-vs-buy-question-we-see-data-leaders-get-wrong.md): Apache Airflow is free to run. What it costs to run well is a different question. Here's how to think through the build vs. buy decision — and what most data leaders get wrong.
- [From Author to Review: Otto Now Covers the Full Dag Lifecycle](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/from-author-to-review-otto-now-covers-the-full-dag-lifecycle.md): Otto runs automatically on every pull request, reviewing your Dag code before a human reviewer ever opens the diff.
- [Investigate Every Pipeline Failure Automatically With Otto](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/investigate-every-pipeline-failure-automatically-with-otto.md): Otto investigates critical failures before you open your laptop
- [Introducing AI-Assisted Migrations with Otto: Your Airflow Expert for the Translation Work that Stalls Every Project](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/introducing-ai-assisted-migrations-with-otto-your-airflow-expert-for-the-translation-work-that-stalls-every-project.md)
- [Airflow in Action: ETL Insights from Bloomberg — Slashing Runtimes by 50%](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-bloomberg-guide-fine-tuning-airflow-production.md): Bloomberg's Data Platform Engineering team shares four real-world Airflow configuration fixes that resolved production issues across 2,500+ DAGs — no code changes required.
- [Why Astronomer Support Is Chasing Michelin Star Service](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/why-astronomer-support-is-chasing-michelin-star-service.md): Astronomer’s Customer Reliability Engineering team was recently honored to receive an award by Business Intelligence Group for our support, a step toward our audacious goal of being the best software support team in the world. We are proud to work with such an incredible customer base, many of whom use Astro for mission-critical workloads. That responsibility demands an uncommon level of service and excellence.
- [Astro Private Cloud 2.0: Disaster Recovery, Governance, and Audit Logging on Your Terms](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/astro-private-cloud-2-0-enterprise-grade-airflow-entirely-within-your-own-environment.md): Astro Private Cloud 2.0 in Generally Available 
- [Airflow in Action: Migrating 200,000 Pipelines to Airflow 3 at Uber](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-uber-2026.md): Uber is migrating 200k pipelines to Airflow 3. Here's the architecture, tooling, and strategy behind one of the largest orchestration migrations ever undertaken.
- [Introducing Otto: The Only Data Engineering Agent Built for Airflow](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/introducing-otto-the-only-data-engineering-agent-built-for-airflow.md): Otto is the only data engineering agent purpose-built for Airflow, and the first to bring Astronomer's depth of operational Airflow knowledge directly to the engineers doing the work.
- [Migrating from airflow-ai-sdk to Apache Airflow's Common AI provider](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/migrating-from-airflow-ai-sdk-to-apache-airflow-s-common-ai-provider.md): apache-airflow-providers-common-ai 0.1.0 shipped in April 2026, Airflow's official provider for AI and LLM workflows, built on PydanticAI and sharing its foundations with the airflow-ai-sdk. Same decorators and engine, plus toolsets that turn 350+ provider hooks into agent tools, durable execution, and built-in human review. Here's what's new, why it matters, and how to migrate without losing a weekend.
- [Cross-Region Disaster Recovery on Astro Is Now Generally Available: Here's How We Built It](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/cross-region-disaster-recovery-on-astro-is-now-generally-available-here-s-how-we-built-it.md): Disaster Recovery on Astro is Generally Available. A look at the architecture decisions, trade-offs, and engineering lessons behind cross-region Disaster Recovery on Astro - from database replication with Aurora Global Clusters to warm standby compute and one-click failover
- [AI Agents Have a Context Problem. It's Hiding in Your Pipelines.](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/ai-agents-have-a-context-problem-it-s-hiding-in-your-pipelines.md): The richest source of context for AI agents already exists in your stack. It's your orchestration layer. Here's why static metadata alone won't get you there.
- [Cosmos 1.14: Battle-Tested Watcher Mode ](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/cosmos-1-14-battle-tested-watcher-mode.md): Cosmos 1.14 delivers significant improvements to Watcher execution mode, the fastest way to run dbt in Airflow.
- [Airflow in Action: Kaiser Permanente's AI Pipelines Detecting Disease Before Clinicians Can](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-kaiser-permanente.md): See how Kaiser Permanente runs AI and ML research pipelines on-prem with Airflow, and how Astronomer supports regulated industries with the same flexibility
- [Airflow in Action: How SAP Delivers Trusted AI for Enterprise Clients](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-sap.md): See how SAP built a production RAG pipeline with Apache Airflow to power Joule for Consultants, processing 5M+ documents across 15 data sources for the enterprise.
- [Introducing Blueprint in Astro: Self-Service Dag Authoring For Your Entire Organization](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/introducing-blueprint-in-astro-self-service-dag-authoring-for-your-entire-organization.md): With Blueprint, creating Airflow pipelines is now possible for anyone in your organization. Data engineers define templates, and others can create pipelines though a drag-and-drop no-code interface in Astro.  No python or Airflow knowledge required. 
- [How Blueprint and Astro IDE Redefine Orchestration](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/how-blueprint-and-astro-ide-redefine-orchestration.md): The final chapter in the Rise of Abstraction series. Blueprint gives platform teams reusable, validated templates. Astro IDE turns them into a visual builder. Together, they close the Airflow literacy gap without sacrificing governance.
- [Introducing Apache Airflow® 3.2](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/apache-airflow-3-2-release.md): Asset partitions, async tasks, and continued improvements to the Airflow 3 platform
- [The EduAgent: The AI Agent Behind Astronomer Academy's Support](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/the-eduagent-the-ai-agent-behind-astronomer-academy-s-support.md): How the Astronomer Education team uses AI to help respond to user tickets and answer questions about Academy usage.
- [Airflow in Action: From Steel City to Data City. Pittsburgh, Astro and Open Government Data](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-pittsburgh.md): See how Pittsburgh's two-person data team uses Apache Airflow and Astro to power open government data, cut manual work, and deliver real civic impact.
- [The AI Agent Behind Astro Runtime's Reliability](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/the-ai-agent-behind-astro-runtimes-reliability.md)
- [Airflow in Action: How DoorDash Scaled for Data and ML Engineering](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-doordash.md): DoorDash runs one of the largest Airflow deployments in the world. See how they built the Orchestration Frederator to scale without the chaos.
- [Airflow in Action: Red Hat's Blueprint for Trusted AI Agents with Astro](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-red-hat.md): How Red Hat built a trusted data and AI platform on Apache Airflow and Astro, powering 95 data products and production AI agents across the enterprise.
- [Build Faster, Let Agents Do More: What's New in the Astro CLI](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/astro-cli-update-march-2026.md): The Astro CLI is the fastest way to develop and deploy Airflow pipelines from your own editor. Today we're making it more powerful with standalone mode, automatic port management, and direct API access that works for both developers and AI coding agents.
- [Airflow in Action: How American Express Orchestrates Metadata Across 3,000 Databases](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-amex.md): Amex runs 100+ production Dags orchestrating metadata with Airflow. See how they built the operators, pipelines, and governance framework that makes it work.
- [Cross-Region Disaster Recovery on Astro: Enterprise Resilience, Without the Engineering Project](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/cross-region-disaster-recovery-on-astro-enterprise-resilience.md): Today, we are announcing the public preview of cross-region Disaster Recovery on Astro, now available on AWS.
- [Improving Reliability with a More Resilient Auth Proxy Architecture](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/improving-reliability-with-a-more-resilient-auth-proxy-architecture.md): Whether you're building new automation or migrating from the beta API, this is the stable foundation you need to programmatically manage Astro at scale.
- [Build Your Data Quality Deck](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/build-your-data-quality-deck.md): Learn how to use Apache Airflow's six SQL check operators to build comprehensive data quality checks for your pipelines, explained through the lens of Magic: The Gathering deck building.
- [Airflow in Action: Boosting BI at Visa. 100% Trust in Data With 70% Lower Overhead](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-visa.md): Visa cut BI dashboard refresh times from 24 hours to 2 hours with Airflow. Learn how they automated end-to-end workflows and achieved zero missed SLAs.
- [Building Kepler](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/building-kepler-astronomer-internal-data-assistant.md): How Astronomer built Kepler, an internal Slackbot and CLI tool that answers ad hoc data questions using LLMs, hybrid search, and code context to democratize data access across the company.
- [What Happens When a PM Runs a Coding Agent (almost) Full-Time](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/what-happens-when-a-pm-runs-a-coding-agent-almost-full-time.md): How our Principal Product Manager used AI coding agents like Claude Code during onboarding to automate workflows, track customer conversations, and ship features in his first 90 days at Astronomer.
- [Airflow in Action: Unlocking Airflow 3's Power for Multi-Tenancy at Datadog](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-datadog.md): Datadog processes 100+ trillion events daily. Learn why they chose Airflow 3 for multi-tenancy, and data-aware scheduling at scale.
- [Dag-Level Roles on Astro: Fine-Grained Access for Enterprise Airflow](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/dag-level-roles-on-astro-fine-grained-access-for-enterprise-airflow.md): Dag-level roles are now available on Astro, giving Enterprise customers the ability to control access to individual Dags within a shared deployment.
- [Airflow in Action: Best Practices Learned From Scaling AI at Oracle](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-oracle.md): Best practices from AI at Oracle: use Airflow to scale GPU-heavy AI and MLOps on Kubernetes with higher reliability, visibility, and GPU ROI.
- [Airflow in Action: Expedia’s Multi-Tenant Platform at 200+ Clusters, 14,000+ Pipelines](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-expedia.md): How Expedia runs 14,000+ Dags across 200+ isolated Airflow clusters with multi-tenancy, templates, and automated CI/CD.
- [Introducing AI Agent Tooling: Bringing Airflow Intelligence to Your Local Workflow](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/introducing-ai-agent-tooling-bringing-airflow-intelligence-to-your-local-workflow.md): Whether you use Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, or any of the 25+ compatible AI coding tools, you can now access specialized Airflow knowledge right where you already work.
- [How to build a decision tracing context graph with Apache Airflow®](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/how-to-build-a-decision-tracing-context-graph-with-apache-airflow.md): Last week, the first-ever in-person Airflow Summit occurred in Toronto, Canada. Over 500 attendees from 20+ countries came together for all things Airflow, orchestration, and open source.
- [The 2026 Astronomer Data Excellence Awards](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/2026-data-excellence-awards.md): This year’s winners span industries, regions, and use cases, but they share a common thread: data orchestration as a strategic advantage.
- [Airflow in Action: Qualcomm Chip Design Orchestration at Million-Task Scale with Airflow 3](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-qualcomm.md): How Qualcomm uses Airflow 3 to orchestrate chip design at massive scale, running millions of EDA tasks daily across global data centers.
- [Introducing Astro API: Production-Ready and Generally Available](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/announcing-astro-api-v1-ga.md): Whether you're building new automation or migrating from the beta API, this is the stable foundation you need to programmatically manage Astro at scale.
- [Airflow in Action: Powering Investigative Journalism at the FT with Orchestration and AI](https://www.astronomer.io/blog/airflow-in-action-financial-times.md): How the Financial Times uses Apache Airflow to orchestrate AI pipelines, structure messy public data, and power investigative journalism at scale.

